{
  "case_id": "2017-16-1215",
  "document_hash": "b2eb95a27a0d39eb030aebbec648ca9dd949286a76fbbdcfc681851a89357e43",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1215",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b2eb95a27a0d39eb030aebbec648ca9dd949286a76fbbdcfc681851a89357e43",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b2eb95a27a0d-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Section 523(a)(2)(A) of the Bankruptcy Code prohibits the discharge of debts procured by fraudulent statements, other than a statement respecting the debtor's financial condition. Everyone agrees that \"financial condition\" is a term of art used by Congress and in commercial practice to refer to one's overall financial status. Yet, Respondent and the government ask this Court to interpret Section 523 and, in particular, Congress's use of \"respecting\" to eliminate the meaning of \"financial condition,\" of a term of art, and essentially to substitute the word \"finances\" for it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1215",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b2eb95a27a0d39eb030aebbec648ca9dd949286a76fbbdcfc681851a89357e43",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b2eb95a27a0d-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Can you tell me, Mr. Garre, what is a statement respecting financial condition? In addition to a balance sheet and a profit and loss statement, what else would qualify?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1215",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b2eb95a27a0d39eb030aebbec648ca9dd949286a76fbbdcfc681851a89357e43",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b2eb95a27a0d-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Could you tell me, Mr. -- Mr. Garre, what you think the difference is between \"relating to\" and \"about\"?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1215",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b2eb95a27a0d39eb030aebbec648ca9dd949286a76fbbdcfc681851a89357e43",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b2eb95a27a0d-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GARRE: So our view, Justice Alito, is this Court should follow what Congress said and say that a statement about a single asset or a single liability is not a statement respecting financial condition. It's just not."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1215",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "b2eb95a27a0d39eb030aebbec648ca9dd949286a76fbbdcfc681851a89357e43",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b2eb95a27a0d-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: May I -- may I ask you to clarify something?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1215",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "b2eb95a27a0d39eb030aebbec648ca9dd949286a76fbbdcfc681851a89357e43",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b2eb95a27a0d-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: But which says more about your financial condition, Mr. Garre?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1215",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "b2eb95a27a0d39eb030aebbec648ca9dd949286a76fbbdcfc681851a89357e43",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b2eb95a27a0d-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The government strenuously argued that the Court should interpret 523(a)(2)(A) in Field in light of that specific problem it was seeking to address."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1215",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "b2eb95a27a0d39eb030aebbec648ca9dd949286a76fbbdcfc681851a89357e43",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b2eb95a27a0d-0001-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The district court and the bankruptcy court both found that not only did the debtor lie about his tax refund -- and I think that the Respondent here has tried to rehabilitate the debtor a little bit."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Hughes",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1215",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "b2eb95a27a0d39eb030aebbec648ca9dd949286a76fbbdcfc681851a89357e43",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b2eb95a27a0d-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. HUGHES: So a few things about that, Your Honor. First, to directly answer your question, we think that the clearest test is to ask: Does the statement describe what would be a line item on one's balance sheet or income statement?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Hughes",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1215",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "b2eb95a27a0d39eb030aebbec648ca9dd949286a76fbbdcfc681851a89357e43",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b2eb95a27a0d-0001-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The rule they set up is, if you put it on the balance sheet, (2)(B) applies, but if you say it standing alone, all of a sudden (2)(A) applies. That's all form and no substance."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1215",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "b2eb95a27a0d39eb030aebbec648ca9dd949286a76fbbdcfc681851a89357e43",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b2eb95a27a0d-0001-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: May I go back to the argument Mr. Garre -- Garre did? He said the Congress was seeking to -- to protect debtors where credit companies were telling them to omit a particular item."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1215",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b2eb95a27a0d39eb030aebbec648ca9dd949286a76fbbdcfc681851a89357e43",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b2eb95a27a0d-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Would you respond to -- to Mr. Garre's argument that the statement here concerns ability to pay and not financial condition?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1215",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b2eb95a27a0d39eb030aebbec648ca9dd949286a76fbbdcfc681851a89357e43",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b2eb95a27a0d-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. HUGHES: Well, it's hard for me to see the distinction between those two, Your Honor, because I think people are concerned about ability-to-pay statements because they go to financial condition, and vice versa, financial condition statements are -- are relevant to condition -- to ability to pay. But, again, as the government says, ability to pay is a very important part of this test. We have two separate amicus briefs who identify a separate way to look at financial condition, which is not just balance sheet solvency but is equitable solvency, which goes to ability to pay."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1215",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b2eb95a27a0d39eb030aebbec648ca9dd949286a76fbbdcfc681851a89357e43",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b2eb95a27a0d-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: What about the argument that you would be putting a burden on small businesses that deal informally? You would be putting a recordkeeping requirement on them for a statement like: I've got this tax refund."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1215",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b2eb95a27a0d39eb030aebbec648ca9dd949286a76fbbdcfc681851a89357e43",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b2eb95a27a0d-0002-0006",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF JEFFREY E. SANDBERG ON BEHALF OF THE UNITED STATES, AS AMICUS CURIAE, IN SUPPORT OF THE RESPONDENT"
    },
